  <data name="Common_Refresh" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Refresh</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Common_Save" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Save</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Control_Severity_Unknown" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unknown</value>
    <comment>[label] Default label of the severity chip control - the small outlined pill with a coloured dot used for drive-health state next to a drive name. Shown when a caller supplies no text, meaning the health state could not be determined. It sits beside Healthy / Warning / Critical, so translate it as a state word, not as 'unknown error'. It must fit in a chip: one short word.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_Action_OpenLatestResults" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Open latest Results</value>
    <comment>[label] Value under the "Recommended next step" caption on the Dashboard hero card when a scan has completed and no drive is short of space. "Results" names the app page of the same name. Not a button.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_Action_RetryScan" xml:space="preserve">
