    <comment>[header] Label on the on/off switch that limits the duplicate-group list to groups containing files that no longer exist on disk since the scan.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Filter_SelectedOnly" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Selected only</value>
    <comment>[header] Label on the on/off switch that limits the duplicate-group list to groups where at least one file is already ticked for deletion.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Group_CanFree" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Can free {0}</value>
    <comment>[label] Line on a duplicate-group row: how much disk space deleting this group's duplicates would free, keeping one file. {0} is an already-formatted size such as '1.4 GB'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Group_FileCount" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} file(s)</value>
    <comment>[label] Count shown on a duplicate-group row: how many files the group contains. {0} is an already-formatted whole number, for example '12'. The '(s)' is the English way of covering singular and plural at once; render it however the target language handles an unknown count.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Group_SelectedCount" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} selected</value>
    <comment>[label] Count shown on a duplicate-group row: how many files in the group are currently ticked for deletion. {0} is an already-formatted whole number.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_IncludeHidden_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Include hidden and system files</value>
    <comment>[header] Label on the on/off switch that lets the duplicate analysis consider files Windows marks as hidden or as system files. Off by default.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_IncludeReparsePoints_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Include reparse points</value>
    <comment>[header] Label on the on/off switch that lets the analysis follow NTFS reparse points (junctions, symbolic links and similar redirections). 'Reparse point' is the Windows term; use the term the German/Spanish Windows documentation uses. Off by default, because following them can make the same file appear twice.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_IncludedFolders_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Included folders</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the multi-line text box listing the only folders the duplicate analysis should look inside. Shown when the scope drop-down is set to included-folder mode.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_KeeperPolicy_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Keep one file by</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the drop-down that decides which single file in each duplicate group is kept while the others are offered for deletion (newest, oldest, shortest path, longest path). The label reads as an unfinished phrase completed by the chosen option. Appears twice on the page: in the run settings and again over the selected group's detail pane.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_LatestRun_None" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No duplicate analysis has been saved for this scan session yet.</value>
    <comment>[status] Helper line under the 'Start analysis' heading when the selected scan session has no stored duplicate run. Tells the user there is nothing to review until Run is pressed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_LatestRun_Summary" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Last run: {0} on {1}. {2} group(s), {3} reclaimable, {4} error(s).</value>
    <comment>[status] Helper line under the 'Start analysis' heading summarising the most recent stored duplicate run. {0} is the run status and stays in English (Completed, Cancelled, Failed); {1} is a date and time already formatted in the user's culture; {2} is an already-formatted group count; {3} an already-formatted size such as '1.4 GB' of space that could be freed; {4} an already-formatted count of errors.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MatchMethods_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Match methods</value>
    <comment>[header] Bold heading over the right-hand column of the Duplicates run settings, where the user turns individual duplicate-detection techniques on and off. 'Match methods' means the ways two files can be judged to be duplicates.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Member_Keeper" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Keeper</value>
    <comment>[status] Status word in the narrow status column of a file row inside a duplicate group. Marks the one file that will be kept; its delete checkbox is disabled. See the glossary entry for 'Keeper (kept duplicate)' - never leave it as the English loanword. Column is about 110 px wide.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Member_Review" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Review</value>
    <comment>[status] Status word in the status column of a file row inside a duplicate group: this copy is neither the keeper nor ticked for deletion, so the user still has to decide about it. Column is about 110 px wide - keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Member_Selected" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Selected</value>
    <comment>[status] Status word in the status column of a file row inside a duplicate group: this copy is ticked and will be deleted when the user runs the deletion. Column is about 110 px wide - keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Members_EmptyState" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Select a group to review members.</value>
    <comment>[empty-state] Message filling the detail pane on the right of the Duplicates page while no duplicate group is selected in the list. 'members' are the individual files belonging to a group.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MethodFilter_All" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>All methods</value>
    <comment>[label] Entry in the 'Method' drop-down that filters the result list on the Duplicates page: show groups found by any detection method. The default.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MethodFilter_Exact" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Exact</value>
    <comment>[label] Entry in the result-list 'Method' filter drop-down: show only groups of byte-identical files. Short form of 'exact match'; keep it short, the drop-down is narrow.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MethodFilter_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Method</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the drop-down that filters the duplicate-group list by the detection method that found each group (exact, normalized text, image pHash, video pHash). Narrow control, keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MethodFilter_ImagePHash" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Image pHash</value>
    <comment>[label] Entry in the result-list 'Method' filter drop-down: show only groups of visually similar images. 'pHash' is the technical name of the perceptual-hash algorithm and stays as-is; only the word 'Image' is translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MethodFilter_NormalizedText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Normalized text</value>
    <comment>[label] Entry in the result-list 'Method' filter drop-down: show only groups of text documents that matched after normalisation (whitespace, casing and formatting ignored) rather than byte-for-byte.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MethodFilter_VideoPHash" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Video pHash</value>
    <comment>[label] Entry in the result-list 'Method' filter drop-down: show only groups of visually similar videos. 'pHash' is the technical name of the perceptual-hash algorithm and stays as-is; only the word 'Video' is translated.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_ExactMatch" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Exact match</value>
    <comment>[label] Method name shown in bold on each duplicate-group row and in the detail pane header: the files in this group are byte-for-byte identical. The safest kind of match.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_ImageReady" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Finds visually similar images.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper line under the 'Similar images' switch, shown when the image-matching component is installed and usable. If it is not, the component's own English reason is shown instead.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_NormalizedEquivalent" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Normalized-equivalent</value>
    <comment>[label] Method name shown on a duplicate-group row: the text documents in this group are equivalent once whitespace, casing and formatting are ignored - not byte-identical. Needs the user's review before deletion.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_PerceptualImage" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Perceptual image match</value>
    <comment>[label] Method name shown on a duplicate-group row: the images in this group look alike to a perceptual-hash comparison (resized, recompressed or lightly edited copies). Needs the user's review before deletion.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_PerceptualVideo" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Perceptual video match</value>
    <comment>[label] Method name shown on a duplicate-group row: the videos in this group look alike to a perceptual-hash comparison. Needs the user's review before deletion.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_SimilarImages_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Similar images</value>
    <comment>[header] Label on the on/off switch that enables perceptual image matching - finding pictures that look alike (resized, recompressed, slightly edited) rather than being byte-identical. Sits in the 'Match methods' box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_SimilarVideos_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Similar videos</value>
    <comment>[header] Label on the on/off switch that enables perceptual video matching - finding videos that look alike rather than being byte-identical. Sits in the 'Match methods' box; needs external tools, see Duplicates_Method_VideoReady.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_TextDocuments_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Text documents</value>
    <comment>[header] Label on the on/off switch that enables matching text documents whose content is equivalent after normalisation (whitespace, casing and formatting ignored), not only byte-identical ones. Sits in the 'Match methods' box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_Unavailable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unavailable.</value>
    <comment>[status] Helper line shown under the 'Similar images' or 'Similar videos' switch when that matching method cannot run on this machine and no more specific reason is available. One word plus a full stop.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Method_VideoReady" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Finds visually similar videos. Needs FFmpeg + ffprobe.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper line under the 'Similar videos' switch, shown when video matching is usable. Warns that it depends on the external FFmpeg tools. 'FFmpeg' and 'ffprobe' are program names and must stay exactly as written, lower-case 'ffprobe' included.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Metric_GroupsFound" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Groups found</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption of the first of four result tiles across the Duplicates page, above a plain count. A 'group' is one set of files judged to be duplicates of each other. Tile is narrow - keep it to two or three words.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Metric_NeedsReview" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Needs review</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption of the third result tile, above the number of groups that matched only approximately and must be checked by the user before anything is deleted. Shown in the warning/amber colour. Narrow tile - keep it very short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Metric_Reclaimable" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Reclaimable</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption of the fourth result tile, above a size such as '4.2 GB': the disk space that would be freed if every duplicate except one keeper per group were deleted. Narrow tile - keep it to one or two words.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Metric_SafeExact" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Safe exact</value>
    <comment>[label] Caption of the second result tile, above the number of groups that are byte-identical matches and can therefore be selected for deletion in bulk. Shown in the healthy/green colour. Narrow tile - keep it very short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MinConfidence_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Min confidence</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the numeric box that hides duplicate groups whose match confidence is below the given value (0 to 1). 'Min' is an abbreviation of minimum - abbreviate in the target language too, the control is narrow.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MinSize_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Min size (MB)</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the numeric box that sets the smallest file size, in megabytes, the duplicate analysis will consider; smaller files are skipped. 'Min' is an abbreviation of minimum - abbreviate in the target language too, the control is narrow. 'MB' stays as-is.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_MoreFilters_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>More filters</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the collapsible section above the duplicate-group list holding the extra filters: sort order, minimum confidence, detection method, and the selected/missing/errored switches.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Page_Automation" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Duplicates page</value>
    <comment>[accessibility] Screen-reader name of the whole Duplicates page. Announced when the page receives focus; never visible on screen. The page itself is titled "Deduplicate" (Duplicates_Title) - this is the name used in the navigation rail, so keep the two consistent with Nav_Duplicates.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Page_Next" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Next</value>
    <comment>[button] Button that steps forward one page in the paged list of duplicate groups. Sits to the right of the page number, next to Duplicates_Page_Previous. Narrow button, keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Page_Previous" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Previous</value>
    <comment>[button] Button that steps back one page in the paged list of duplicate groups. Sits to the left of the page number, next to Duplicates_Page_Next. Narrow button, keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_PathList_Placeholder" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>One path per line</value>
    <comment>[placeholder] Grey hint text inside the empty included-folders and excluded-folders boxes on the Duplicates page. Tells the user the expected input format: one filesystem folder path on each line. 'path' means a folder location such as C:\Users\Ada\Pictures.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_ScanSession_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scan session</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the drop-down that picks which completed scan run the duplicate analysis reads its file list from. 'Scan session' is one finished scan of a folder tree; the list shows each session's root path.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_ScopeFilters_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Folder scope and file filters</value>
    <comment>[header] Header of the collapsible section holding the included-folder list, the excluded-folder list and the custom extension list. Collapsed by default.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_ScopeHelp_ExcludedFolders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Everything in scan is checked except listed folders and global exclusions.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper sentence under the scope drop-down, shown while the scope is set to excluded folders. Says that the whole scan is analysed apart from the paths in the 'Excluded folders' box plus the exclusion list configured application-wide in Settings.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_ScopeHelp_IncludedFolders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Only files inside listed folders are checked.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper sentence under the scope drop-down on the Duplicates page, shown while the scope is set to included folders. 'listed folders' are the paths the user typed into the 'Included folders' box.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_ScopeHelp_WholeSession" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Whole completed scan is checked.</value>
    <comment>[description] Helper sentence under the scope drop-down, shown while the scope is set to the whole session: every file recorded by the selected completed scan is analysed.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Scope_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Scope</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the drop-down that chooses how much of the scan is analysed: the whole session, only listed folders, or everything except listed folders. Narrow control, keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Search_Placeholder" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Search filename or path</value>
    <comment>[placeholder] Grey hint text inside the empty search box above the list of duplicate groups. Typing there narrows the list to groups whose file name or folder path contains the text.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_SelectedSummary" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} file(s) selected on current page</value>
    <comment>[status] Summary of how many files are currently ticked for deletion on the displayed page of duplicate groups. {0} is an already-formatted count.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Sort_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sort</value>
    <comment>[header] Header above the drop-down that chooses the order the duplicate groups are listed in (for example most reclaimable space first). Narrow control, keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_StartAnalysis_Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Start analysis</value>
    <comment>[header] Bold heading over the left-hand settings block on the Duplicates page (scan session, file type, minimum size, scope, keeper policy). Labels the group of choices made before pressing Run.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_Cancelled" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Analysis cancelled.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after a duplicate analysis was stopped by the user. Results found before the stop are kept.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_Cancelling" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cancelling…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line between the user pressing Cancel and the running analysis actually stopping. Ends with a horizontal-ellipsis character in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_ChooseSession" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose a completed scan session to review duplicates.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line when no scan session is selected in the drop-down yet. Only completed scans can be analysed for duplicates.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_ClearedSelections" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Cleared selections on page {0}.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after the 'Deselect page' command unticked everything on the displayed page. {0} is the already-formatted page number.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_DeleteDone" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0} from page {1}.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after duplicates were deleted with no problems. {0} is one of the Safety_Duplicates_Outcome_* fragments, for example 'Moved 820 MB across 40 file(s) to quarantine'; {1} is the already-formatted page number the files came from. This key supplies only the tail of the sentence, so keep it grammatical after whichever fragment precedes it.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_DeleteErrors" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0}; {1} group(s) failed. First error: {2}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after a deletion in which whole groups could not be processed. {0} is one of the Safety_Duplicates_Outcome_* fragments describing what did succeed, {1} an already-formatted count of failed groups, {2} the first error's technical text, which stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_DeleteErrorsAndWarnings" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0}; {1} group(s) failed and {2} bookkeeping warning(s). First issue: {3}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after a deletion that had both failed groups and incomplete bookkeeping. {0} is one of the Safety_Duplicates_Outcome_* fragments, {1} an already-formatted count of failed groups, {2} an already-formatted count of warnings, {3} the first error's technical text, which stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_DeleteWarnings" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0}; {1} bookkeeping warning(s). First warning: {2}</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after duplicates were deleted but some database bookkeeping did not go through - the files were handled, the record-keeping was incomplete. {0} is one of the Safety_Duplicates_Outcome_* fragments, {1} an already-formatted count, {2} the first warning's technical text, which stays in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_Initial" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose scan session, run duplicate analysis, review groups, delete copies.</value>
    <comment>[status] First status line at the bottom of the Duplicates page, before anything has been loaded. Names the four steps of the workflow in order. Reads as a terse instruction list, not a full sentence.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_LoadedGroupsForReview" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Loaded page {0} of {1} duplicate group(s). Review before deleting.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after a duplicate analysis finishes with results. {0} is the page number now displayed and {1} the total number of groups found, both already formatted. The closing instruction to review before deleting must be kept.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_LoadedGroupsPage" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Loaded page {0} of duplicate groups ({1} total).</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after the stored results of an earlier duplicate run were loaded. {0} is the page number displayed and {1} the total number of groups, both already formatted.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_LoadedPage" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Loaded page {0}.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after the user stepped to another page of the duplicate-group list with Previous or Next. {0} is the already-formatted page number.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_LoadingReview" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Loading duplicate review data…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line while the page loads the latest duplicate run, its groups and its errors from the database. Ends with a horizontal-ellipsis character in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_NeedCustomExtension" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Enter at least one custom extension for custom-scope dedupe.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line shown when Run was pressed with the file type set to custom extensions but the extension box left empty. 'dedupe' is the short form of deduplication - use the glossary term rather than a loanword.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_NeedIncludedFolders" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Add one or more folder prefixes for included-folder scope.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line shown when Run was pressed with the scope set to included folders but no path listed. A 'folder prefix' is the start of a path, so C:\Photos covers everything beneath it.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_NoGroups" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No duplicate groups found for current scope.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after a duplicate analysis finishes having found nothing, given the chosen scope, file type and minimum size. Good news, not an error.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_NoRunYet" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No duplicate analysis has been run for this scan yet.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line when the selected scan session exists but duplicate analysis has never been run over it. The remedy is the Run button.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_Progress" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>{0}: {1} / {2} ({3} groups, {4} errors)</value>
    <comment>[status] Live progress line while duplicate analysis runs. {0} is the current phase name supplied by the engine and stays in English (for example 'Hashing exact candidates'); {1} is files processed and {2} the total for that phase; {3} is duplicate groups found so far and {4} the number of files that could not be read. All five arrive already formatted - translate only the words 'groups' and 'errors' and keep the punctuation layout.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_RunHadNoGroups" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Latest duplicate analysis completed without duplicate groups.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line when the most recent stored duplicate run finished successfully but found no duplicates at all.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_SelectSessionAndType" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Select a scan session and file type before running duplicate analysis.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line shown when Run was pressed without a scan session or a file type chosen. Names both missing choices.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_SelectedExactOnPage" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Selected exact-match duplicates on page {0}.</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line after the 'Select safe exact (page)' command ticked every byte-identical duplicate on the displayed page. {0} is the already-formatted page number.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Status_Starting" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Starting duplicate analysis…</value>
    <comment>[status] Status line at the moment the Run button is pressed, before the first progress report arrives. Ends with a horizontal-ellipsis character in English.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Subtitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Grouped review, keeper policies, and recoverable deletion defaults.</value>
    <comment>[description] One-line subtitle under the "Deduplicate" page title. Summarises the page in three phrases: duplicates are reviewed in groups; a 'keeper policy' decides which file in each group is kept; and deletion defaults to a recoverable route (Recycle Bin or quarantine) rather than a permanent one.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Duplicates_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Deduplicate</value>
    <comment>[title] Main title in the header bar at the top of the Duplicates page (titled "Deduplicate"), where the user reviews groups of duplicate files found in a completed scan and deletes the copies. It is a verb/activity name, not a plural noun: the page is where the user removes duplicate files. Sits beside Duplicates_Subtitle in a single-line header, so keep it short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DriveHealthStatus_Critical" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Critical</value>
    <comment>[label] Drive health badge caption for a failing drive.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DriveHealthStatus_Healthy" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Healthy</value>
    <comment>[label] Drive health badge caption for a drive with no reported problem.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DriveHealthStatus_Unknown" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Unknown</value>
    <comment>[label] Drive health badge caption when the drive reports nothing usable.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DriveHealthStatus_Unsupported" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Not supported</value>
    <comment>[label] Drive health badge caption when the drive cannot report health at all.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DriveHealthStatus_Warning" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Warning</value>
    <comment>[label] Drive health badge caption for a drive reporting a warning.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DuplicateGroupSortBy_ConfidenceDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Highest confidence</value>
    <comment>[label] Duplicate group sort order: most certain matches first.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DuplicateGroupSortBy_LatestModifiedDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Most recently modified</value>
    <comment>[label] Duplicate group sort order: most recently changed first.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DuplicateGroupSortBy_MemberCountDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Most copies</value>
    <comment>[label] Duplicate group sort order: largest groups first.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DuplicateGroupSortBy_Method" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Detection method</value>
    <comment>[label] Duplicate group sort order: grouped by detection method.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Enum_DuplicateGroupSortBy_ReclaimableBytesDesc" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Most space to reclaim</value>
    <comment>[label] Duplicate group sort order: most reclaimable space first.</comment>
  </data>
